<item>
<title>[WAB-2786] UK-US-1.2.3 Identity Check for UK Residents</title>
<link>https://jira.andersenlab.com/browse/WAB-2786</link>
<project id="33855" key="WAB">WaBank</project>
<description><p><b>As a</b> visitor (<a href="https://wiki.andersenlab.com/display/SMH/Glossary+for+UK" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">UK-T-1</a>),</p> <p><b>I want</b> verify my identity by uploading a passport copy and taking a selfie,</p> <p><b>So that</b> I can proceed with registration.</p> <p> </p> <p><a href="https://wiki.andersenlab.com/display/SMH/UK-US-1.2.3+Identity+Check+for+UK+Residents" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">UK-US-1.2.3 Identity Check for UK Residents</a></p> <p> </p> <ol> <li>The User sees an upload field with the following configuration:</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Upload field is inactive until a file is added</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Placeholder text: <em>"Choose a file or drop it here (PDF or PNG)"</em></li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Hint below the field: <em>"Please upload the copy of your BRC/ BRD or passport page containing your photo"</em></li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Supported formats: .PDF, .PNG</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Maximum file size: 5 MB</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li>The User can upload the file either from the device’s file system (e.g., File Explorer on desktop, file picker on mobile devices) or by dragging and dropping the file into the upload area</li> </ol> <ol> <li>Uploaded file validation rules:</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>If file format is not supported, system displays: <em>"Unsupported file format"</em></li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>If file exceeds 5MB, system displays: <em>"File exceeds the 5MB limit"</em></li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li>If file is valid:</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Upload field becomes active</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>A loading indicator appears when upload starts</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Upon upload completion, the system confirms upload success</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li>If validation fails during upload (e.g., corrupted file or technical error):</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The system displays a message: <em>"Upload failed. Please try again or use a different document."</em></li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>File is not stored</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The User can retry upload</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li>Upon successful upload:</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>File is stored on the backend</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Backend system is used for recognition</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li>If the User was granted a permission before 31 October 2024 - the system extracts BRC/BRP Unique number from the document</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>It compares extracted value with data entered in (<a href="https://wiki.andersenlab.com/display/SMH/UK-US-1.1.5+Choosing+User%27s+status+in+the+UK+and+ID+document" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">UK-US-1.1.5</a>)</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>If the match is 100%, the User becomes able to proceed to the next selfie step</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>If match is less than 100%:</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The system displays: <em>"The information in the attached file doesn’t match ones you have entered to the Application form. Please check your information in the Application form or upload the document again. You will be redirected to the previous step in 30 seconds."</em></li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Clear uploaded file</li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The User can go back to the previous step</li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>If the User is inactive, redirect to <a href="https://wiki.andersenlab.com/display/SMH/UK-US-1.1.5+Choosing+User%27s+status+in+the+UK+and+ID+document" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">UK-US-1.1.5</a> after 30 seconds</li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li>If the User was granted a permission after 31 October 2024 and provided an <a href="https://wiki.andersenlab.com/display/SMH/Data+Dictionary+for+UK#DataDictionaryforUK-eVisa" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">eVisa shared code</a>, the system performs a validation via the <a href="https://user-auth.apply-to-visit-or-stay-in-the-uk.homeoffice.gov.uk/auth/realms/ExternalChecker/protocol/openid-connect/auth?state=eb845c937da4de45159e4ede3d5157d1&amp;client_id=external-checker-rtwr&amp;nonce=b4fce29737270e748500d862f7f818b4&amp;response_type=code&amp;redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fright-to-work.service.gov.uk%2Frtw-view%2Fchecker-details%2Fredirection&amp;scope=openid%20email%20profile" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Home Office's online checking service</a></li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The system verifies that:</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The code complies with validation rules (<a href="https://wiki.andersenlab.com/display/SMH/Data+Dictionary+for+UK#DataDictionaryforUK-eVisa" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">EL-09</a>)</li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The immigration status allows using banking services</li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> If status is not approved:</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The User sees notification: <em>"Your immigration status does not allow you to apply for banking services. Please contact UKVI Support."</em></li> <li>The registration stops. Next verification steps become unavailable</li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> <li>After successful validation, the system requests User the camera access</li> </ol> <ol> <li>If the User doesn't grant access to the camera:</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The system displays: <em>"To proceed with identity verification, camera access is required. Please enable camera access in your browser or device settings."</em></li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The selfie step becomes blocked until access is granted</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The User has options to:</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Retry camera access request</li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Cancel the identity verification and return to the main page</li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li>If the User gives access to the device's camera:</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The User sees a camera frame</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Field mask: UI guideline showing where the face should be positioned</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Field hint: <em>"Check a camera on your device is on. Look directly at the camera and make a photo."</em></li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The User takes a photo by clicking the appropriate button on the field</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li>The User can preview the selfie after it's taken:</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>They have an option to:</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Confirm upload</li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Retake the photo</li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li>If the User confirms the selfie upload, the uploaded photo is temporarily stored in the backend</li> </ol> <ol> <li>If the User decides to retake photo, the previous selfie is automatically discarded and replaced</li> </ol> <ol> <li>The system compares the uploaded selfie photo with the uploaded passport or residence document photo</li> </ol> <ol> <li>Identity validation:</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>If match is ≥ 90%:</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Identity is verified - the system redirects User to next step <a href="https://wiki.andersenlab.com/display/SMH/UK-US-1.1.6+Creating+password+and+completing+registration" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">UK-US-1.1.6 Creating password and completing registration</a></li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>If match is &lt; 90%:</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The system shows an error: <em>"Your identity was not proved. You can upload your BRC/ BRD or passport copy and make selfie once again and try to proceed again."</em></li> <li>The User can retry to upload passport and/or selfie</li> </ol> </li> </ol> </li> <li>The User has the ability to:</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Return to the previous page (<a href="https://wiki.andersenlab.com/display/SMH/UK-US-1.1.5+Choosing+User%27s+status+in+the+UK+and+ID+document" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">UK-US-1.1.5</a>)</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>Cancel the registration process</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li>If the User refreshes the page:</li> </ol> <ol> <li> <ol> <li>The uploaded document/photo remain saved</li> </ol> </li> </ol> <ol> <li> </li> </ol> </description>
